{
 "mechanism": "Level-1 behaviour-set radial coordinates on top of the unchanged RQ-VAE baseline. Once, from the Stage-2 TRAINING split only, the mechanism counts directed within-sequence item pairs n_ij (i != j, self-loops excluded) and forms the two directed marginals n_i = sum_j n_ij (out-degree) and n'_j = sum_i n_ij (in-degree); the idea's symbol n_j in the threshold n_ij > n_i n_j / M denotes this in-degree marginal n'_j, which is the only reading under which n_i n'_j / M is the popularity-only expectation, and this definitional choice propagates into s_i, b_bar, R and every radius. It sets S_i = { j : n_ij > n_i n'_j / M }, s_i = |S_i|, T_i = log(1+s_i), b_bar = mean_i s_i, T_bar = mean_i T_i, and freezes the global scalars R = max(1, log(N_items)/log(1+max(b_bar,1.1))), kappa = -1/R^2 (i.e. c = 1/R^2 in the contract, whose ball radius is R_c = 1/sqrt(c) = R) and T_max = 2R atanh(0.95). R is one global frozen scalar shared by all items, not a per-item quantity. At every training step, for level 1 only, zhat = z/max(||z||, eps) with eps = 1e-8, Te = min(T_i_eff, T_max) where T_i_eff = T_i[item_id] (or T_bar when USE_BEHAV=False) and item_id is the target item whose level-1 token must be identified, u_i = r_i zhat_i with r_i = R tanh(Te/(2R)) = (Te/2) tanhc(Te/(2R)), so d_c(0,u_i) = 2R artanh(r_i/R) = min(T_i_eff, T_max) (not T_i_eff when the clamp binds), and every level-1 codeword is transported to c_k = exp_0^c(e_k/2) = R tanh(||e_k||/(2R)) e_k/||e_k|| = (e_k/2) tanhc(||e_k||/(2R)) with tanhc(0) := 1. The level-1 token is k1 = argmin_k d_c(u_i,c_k), where d_c is exactly the contract's distance, d_c(u,c) = (2/sqrt c) artanh(sqrt c ||(-u) (+) c||) = R arccosh(1 + 2R^2 ||u-c||^2/((R^2-||u||^2)(R^2-||c||^2))), with no epsilon floor in the denominator (the bare arccosh is only an argmin-equivalent rescaling of the contract distance and is not used). Then z_q1 = e_{k1} = E1[k1] is the Euclidean codeword (never c_{k1}, never u_i), res_1 = z - z_q1 is unchanged, and levels 2..L run the baseline Euclidean residual argmin with no curvature, no radii, no Sinkhorn, no temperature. The decoder receives the straight-through vector z_st = z + (z_q - z).detach() with z_q = sum_l e^{(l)}_{k_l} = z - res_L, whose numerical value is the sum of Euclidean codewords, level 1 contributing E1[k1]. The metric only decides the integer k1 and carries no gradient; the backward is stated once, dL/dz = dL_rec/dz_st (identity through the detach) + 2 beta sum_{l=1..L} (res_{l-1} - e^{(l)}_{k_l}), with res_0 = z, and the codebook rows get the baseline codebook and commitment gradients at the fixed indices. The loss, decoder, interfaces, beta and optimizer are the baseline ones; there is no extra loss term, no extra hyperparameter, no temperature, no clip bound and no Sinkhorn.",
 "computations": [
  {
   "name": "pair_counts",
   "definition": "n_ij = number of ordered pairs (a,b) with a = i and b = j at consecutive positions of one TRAINING-split sequence of a training user, i != j; self-loops are excluded and validation/test sequences are never read",
   "inputs": [
    "training_sequences (Stage-2 TRAINING split only)"
   ],
   "output": "N_items x N_items int64 count matrix (sparse)",
   "differentiable": false,
   "note": "precomputed once and frozen before the first training step"
  },
  {
   "name": "item_marginals",
   "definition": "n_i = sum_j n_ij (out-degree of i) and n'_j = sum_i n_ij (in-degree of j); self-loops are excluded from both marginals",
   "inputs": [
    "n_ij"
   ],
   "output": "two length-N_items int64 vectors",
   "differentiable": false,
   "note": "the idea writes S_i = { j : n_ij > n_i n_j / M } with a single item-count vector; its n_j is defined here as the in-degree marginal n'_j, the only reading under which n_i n'_j / M is the popularity-only expectation. This is a definitional decision and it propagates into s_i, T_i, b_bar, R and every radius"
  },
  {
   "name": "total_transitions",
   "definition": "M = sum_i sum_j n_ij",
   "inputs": [
    "n_ij"
   ],
   "output": "scalar int64",
   "differentiable": false,
   "note": "denominator of the popularity-only expectation"
  },
  {
   "name": "adjusted_successor_set",
   "definition": "S_i = { j : n_ij > n_i n'_j / M }, evaluated in exact integer arithmetic by multiplying through by M (strict >, no epsilon, no tie tolerance)",
   "inputs": [
    "n_ij",
    "n_i",
    "n'_j",
    "M"
   ],
   "output": "N_items sets",
   "differentiable": false,
   "note": "co-consumption above the popularity-only expectation; the mechanism's only notion of a behaviour edge"
  },
  {
   "name": "adjusted_out_degree",
   "definition": "s_i = |S_i|",
   "inputs": [
    "S_i"
   ],
   "output": "length-N_items int64",
   "differentiable": false,
   "note": "the behaviour signal is this one scalar per item"
  },
  {
   "name": "behaviour_signal",
   "definition": "T_i = log(1 + s_i)",
   "inputs": [
    "s_i"
   ],
   "output": "length-24556 float32 buffer",
   "differentiable": false,
   "note": "frozen; the only per-item behaviour quantity that reaches the forward pass"
  },
  {
   "name": "catalogue_moments",
   "definition": "b_bar = (1/N_items) sum_i s_i ; T_bar = (1/N_items) sum_i T_i",
   "inputs": [
    "s_i",
    "T_i",
    "N_items"
   ],
   "output": "two float64 scalars",
   "differentiable": false,
   "note": "N_items = 24556; T_bar is the value USE_BEHAV=False substitutes for every T_i"
  },
  {
   "name": "curvature_radius",
   "definition": "R = max(1, log(N_items)/log(1 + max(b_bar, 1.1))) ; c = 1/R^2 ; kappa = -c = -1/R^2 ; T_max = 2 R atanh(0.95) = R log(39) (since atanh(0.95) = 0.5 log(39))",
   "inputs": [
    "b_bar",
    "N_items"
   ],
   "output": "float64 scalars R, c, kappa, T_max",
   "differentiable": false,
   "note": "R is ONE global frozen scalar shared by all items, not a per-item quantity; the contract ball radius is R_c = 1/sqrt(c) = R and the contract forbids a fixed 0.999 clamp"
  },
  {
   "name": "radius_table",
   "definition": "T_i_eff = T_i if USE_BEHAV else T_bar (for every i) ; Te_i = min(T_i_eff, T_max) ; r_i = R tanh(Te_i/(2R)) = (Te_i/2) tanhc(Te_i/(2R)) with tanhc(x) = tanh(x)/x and tanhc(0) = 1",
   "inputs": [
    "T_i",
    "T_bar",
    "T_max",
    "R",
    "USE_BEHAV"
   ],
   "output": "length-24556 float32 buffers r and T_i_eff",
   "differentiable": false,
   "note": "frozen buffers. The exact identities are r_i = ||exp_0^c((min(T_i_eff,T_max)/2) zhat)|| and d_c(0,u_i) = 2R artanh(r_i/R) = min(T_i_eff, T_max); d_c(0,u_i) = T_i_eff only for items with T_i_eff <= T_max, otherwise the clamp binds at T_max = R log(39) = 3.6636 R. r_i <= 0.95 R < R for every item"
  },
  {
   "name": "gather_item_radius",
   "definition": "r_i = r[item_id] and T_i_eff = T_eff[item_id], with item_id the TARGET item of the example (the item whose level-1 token must be identified), not the last history item and not an aggregate of the history",
   "inputs": [
    "r buffer",
    "T_eff buffer",
    "item_id (B,) int64"
   ],
   "output": "B float32 each",
   "differentiable": false,
   "note": "integer lookup; no gradient into the buffer, none with respect to item_id. The choice of item_id is part of the mechanism: the per-item radial coordinate is applied to the target item"
  },
  {
   "name": "normalise_query",
   "definition": "zhat = z / max(||z||_2, eps), eps = 1e-8",
   "inputs": [
    "z (B x 32)",
    "eps"
   ],
   "output": "B x 32",
   "differentiable": true,
   "note": "the eps branch is only a numerical guard; for ||z|| > eps the gradient is (I - zhat zhat^T)/||z||"
  },
  {
   "name": "transport_query",
   "definition": "u_i = r_i zhat_i (equivalently u_i = exp_0^c((Te_i/2) zhat_i), the origin exponential of the contract); no projection is applied",
   "inputs": [
    "zhat",
    "r_i",
    "R",
    "T_max"
   ],
   "output": "B x 32",
   "differentiable": true,
   "note": "||u_i|| = r_i <= 0.95 R < (1-eps_c) R with eps_c = 1e-6, so the contract projection would be the identity and is omitted from the mechanism; c ||u_i||^2 <= 0.9025 < 1"
  },
  {
   "name": "code_transport",
   "definition": "ne_k = ||e_k||_2 ; tc_k = ne_k/(2R) ; tanhc(x) = tanh(x)/x for x != 0 and tanhc(0) := 1 ; rho_k = R tanh(tc_k) = (ne_k/2) tanhc(tc_k) ; c_k = rho_k e_k/ne_k = (e_k/2) tanhc(tc_k), and c_k = e_k/2 explicitly when ne_k = 0",
   "inputs": [
    "E1 (256 x 32, Euclidean, unchanged)",
    "R"
   ],
   "output": "256 x 32 float64",
   "differentiable": true,
   "note": "this is exp_0^c(e_k/2) by the contract; ||c_k|| = rho_k < R for all finite ||e_k||, so c ||c_k||^2 < 1. The explicit branch at ne_k = 0 has value c_k = 0 and Jacobian 0.5 I, matching the limit of the formula; there is no eps guard and no NaN"
  },
  {
   "name": "level1_distance",
   "definition": "d_ik = d_c(u_i, c_k) = (2/sqrt c) artanh(sqrt c ||(-u_i) (+) c_k||) = R arccosh(1 + 2 R^2 ||u_i - c_k||^2 / ((R^2 - ||u_i||^2)(R^2 - ||c_k||^2))), with c = 1/R^2, u_i and c_k the transported points above, denominator in float64 and NO epsilon floor",
   "inputs": [
    "u_i (B x 32)",
    "c_k (256 x 32)",
    "R"
   ],
   "output": "B x 256 float64",
   "differentiable": true,
   "note": "this is exactly the contract distance in the kappa = -1/R^2 parameterisation; the outer factor R is the contract's (2/sqrt c) and is a single global frozen scalar. The bare arccosh is an argmin-equivalent rescaling and is not computed. (R^2 - ||u_i||^2) >= (1 - 0.95^2) R^2 = 0.0975 R^2 because r_i <= 0.95R, and (R^2 - ||c_k||^2) > 0 because ||c_k|| < R; hence the denominator is strictly positive and the exact formula is used, with no 1e-6 R^4 floor. If ||e_k|| is so large that tanh(tc_k) rounds to 1.0 in float64, the denominator underflows to 0 and d_ik = +inf, which is the correct limit of the contract distance as ||c_k|| -> R; the argmin then never selects that code"
  },
  {
   "name": "level1_assignment",
   "definition": "k1 = argmin_{k in 0..255} d_ik, ties resolved to the smallest index k",
   "inputs": [
    "d (B x 256)"
   ],
   "output": "B int64",
   "differentiable": false,
   "note": "the behaviour's entry point into the model; the only place the level-1 token is decided, and it carries no gradient. d is detached before the argmin"
  },
  {
   "name": "level1_quantized",
   "definition": "z_q1 = E1[k1] = e_{k1}",
   "inputs": [
    "E1",
    "k1"
   ],
   "output": "B x 32",
   "differentiable": true,
   "note": "the INDEX k1 is non-differentiable; the gathered codeword is differentiable with respect to its codebook row E1[k1] (scatter-add of the codebook and commitment gradients) and has no gradient with respect to k1. The decoder never sees c_{k1} and never sees u_i"
  },
  {
   "name": "residual_level1",
   "definition": "res_1 = z - z_q1",
   "inputs": [
    "z",
    "z_q1"
   ],
   "output": "B x 32",
   "differentiable": true,
   "note": "baseline formula, unchanged. dres_1/dz = I and dres_1/dE1[k1] = -I; res_1 is differentiable with respect to z and with respect to E1[k1]"
  },
  {
   "name": "deep_levels",
   "definition": "for l = 2..L: k_l = argmin_k ||res_{l-1} - e^{(l)}_k||_2 ; res_l = res_{l-1} - e^{(l)}_{k_l}",
   "inputs": [
    "res_1",
    "E_2..E_L",
    "L"
   ],
   "output": "k_l (B,) int64 and res_l (B x 32) for each l",
   "differentiable": true,
   "note": "exactly baseline: no curvature, no radii, no Sinkhorn, no temperature, interface untouched. The indices k_l are non-differentiable; each gathered codeword e^{(l)}_{k_l} is differentiable with respect to its codebook E_l; each res_l is differentiable with respect to z and with respect to the earlier gathered codewords e^{(m)}_{k_m}, m <= l"
  },
  {
   "name": "straight_through",
   "definition": "z_q = sum_{l=1..L} e^{(l)}_{k_l} = z - res_L ; z_st = z + (z_q - z).detach()",
   "inputs": [
    "z",
    "e^{(l)}_{k_l} for l = 1..L"
   ],
   "output": "B x 32",
   "differentiable": true,
   "note": "the baseline RQ-VAE/VQ-VAE straight-through convention is pinned here: numerically z_st = z_q, and in the backward dz_st/dz = I while dz_st/dz_q = 0, so the reconstruction reaches the encoder by the identity and reaches no codebook. This is the baseline straight-through, unchanged, and it is the only reconstruction gradient path to z"
  },
  {
   "name": "total_loss",
   "definition": "L = L_rec(D(z_st), x) + sum_{l=1..L} ( ||sg[res_{l-1}] - e^{(l)}_{k_l}||_2^2 + beta ||res_{l-1} - sg[e^{(l)}_{k_l}]||_2^2 ), with res_0 := z, sg the stop-gradient, and beta = 0.25 the baseline commitment weight",
   "inputs": [
    "x",
    "decoder D",
    "z_st",
    "res_{l-1}",
    "e^{(l)}_{k_l}"
   ],
   "output": "scalar",
   "differentiable": true,
   "note": "baseline RQ-VAE objective, unmodified: reconstruction + codebook + commit; no extra term, no extra hyperparameter, no temperature, no clip bound, no Sinkhorn"
  },
  {
   "name": "switch_behaviour",
   "definition": "USE_BEHAV = True: T_i_eff = T_i ; USE_BEHAV = False: T_i_eff = T_bar for every i (and every other quantity, including b_bar, R, c, T_max, is left as precomputed)",
   "inputs": [
    "USE_BEHAV",
    "T_i",
    "T_bar"
   ],
   "output": "T_i_eff (length 24556) feeding radius_table",
   "differentiable": false,
   "note": "the behaviour ablation; not trained in this round"
  },
  {
   "name": "switch_geometry",
   "definition": "USE_CURV = True: the Poincare branch above with c = 1/R^2 ; USE_CURV = False: the exact c -> 0 limit r_i = Te_i/2, u_i = (Te_i/2) zhat_i, c_k = e_k/2, d_ik = 2 ||u_i - c_k||_2 = ||Te_i zhat_i - e_k||_2, with Te_i = min(T_i_eff, T_max) and T_max = 2R atanh(0.95) diverging as c -> 0, so in this branch Te_i = T_i_eff and no radial clamp applies",
   "inputs": [
    "USE_CURV",
    "zhat",
    "e_k",
    "T_i_eff"
   ],
   "output": "the B x 256 matrix the argmin consumes",
   "differentiable": false,
   "note": "the c = 0 branch is a first-class Euclidean metric of the contract (d_0(x,y) = 2||x-y||); nothing is dropped: 2||(Te/2) zhat - e/2|| = ||Te zhat - e||. At ||e_k|| = 0 this branch gives c_k = e_k/2 exactly, the same value and Jacobian as the curved branch's tanhc(0) = 1, so the branches agree at the origin"
  }
 ],
 "inputs": [
  "encoder output z (B x 32)",
  "item_id (B,) int64, the target item of each example whose level-1 token must be identified",
  "level-1 codebook E1 (256 x 32, Euclidean, unchanged)",
  "deeper codebooks E_2..E_L (baseline, Euclidean)",
  "frozen per-item buffers r (24556 float32) and T_i_eff (24556 float32)",
  "frozen scalars R, c = 1/R^2, kappa = -1/R^2, T_max = 2R atanh(0.95), b_bar, T_bar",
  "Stage-2 TRAINING-split sequences (once only, to form n_ij, n_i, n'_j, M, S_i, s_i, T_i)",
  "target item x and decoder D for the baseline loss",
  "flags USE_BEHAV, USE_CURV, eps = 1e-8, eps_c = 1e-6"
 ],
 "outputs": [
  "level-1 code index k1 (B,) int64",
  "the Euclidean codeword e_{k1} = E1[k1] (B x 32), used both for the straight-through reconstruction and as the subtrahend of the residual handed to the baseline deep levels",
  "deeper indices k_2..k_L (B,) and their summed codeword z_q in the baseline format",
  "no change to any deeper level's interface, to the decoder, or to the Stage-3 input format"
 ],
 "parameters": [
  "n_ij, n_i, n'_j, M (frozen integer tables)",
  "s_i, T_i (24556 float32, frozen), b_bar, T_bar (frozen float64 scalars)",
  "R, c = 1/R^2, kappa = -1/R^2, T_max = 2R atanh(0.95) (frozen float64 scalars)",
  "r_i and T_i_eff (24556 float32, frozen)",
  "USE_BEHAV (bool), USE_CURV (bool)",
  "E1 (256 x 32) trainable with baseline init and baseline codebook update",
  "E_2..E_L and decoder D trainable, baseline",
  "beta = 0.25 (baseline commitment weight)",
  "eps = 1e-8 (normalisation guard); eps_c = 1e-6 (value of the contract projection epsilon; unused because no point is ever projected)"
 ],
 "switches": [
  "USE_BEHAV = False (ablation behaviour off): T_i_eff = T_bar for every item, so r_i = R tanh(min(T_bar,T_max)/(2R)) is the same for all items and d_c(0,u_i) = min(T_bar,T_max); the level-1 assignment becomes a curvature-only angular metric with no per-item branching resolution. Same code, one flag, not trained in this round; b_bar, R, c and T_max stay at their precomputed values",
  "USE_CURV = False (ablation geometry off): the exact c -> 0 limit of the same block is used, r_i = Te_i/2, u_i = (Te_i/2) zhat_i, c_k = e_k/2 and d_ik = 2 ||u_i - c_k||_2 = ||Te_i zhat_i - e_k||_2; because T_max = 2R atanh(0.95) -> infinity as c -> 0, this branch has Te_i = T_i_eff and no radial clamp. At ||e_k|| = 0 it gives c_k = e_k/2 exactly, the same value and Jacobian as the curved branch's tanhc(0) = 1. Same code, one flag, not trained in this round; R, c, kappa and T_max are not used numerically in this branch"
 ],
 "excluded": [
  "Sinkhorn, optimal transport and any discrete prior over codes: the level-1 token is a plain per-item argmin and the specification forbids Sinkhorn",
  "temperature, annealing, Gumbel noise, a soft or relaxed argmin, and any gradient through the assignment: the token is a hard argmin and the metric carries no gradient",
  "a clip bound on the distance or on the radii other than T_max, and any fixed 0.999 unit-ball clamp: the contract forbids a fixed clamp when c != 1, and the only clamp is T_max = 2R atanh(0.95) on the radius",
  "an epsilon floor in the Poincare denominator: the exact contract distance is used, with the denominator strictly positive because ||u_i|| <= 0.95 R and ||c_k|| < R",
  "clamping or rescaling the codewords to enforce ||e_k|| <= T_max: the codebook stays Euclidean and unchanged, and codewords with ||e_k|| > T_max are allowed; their transported points satisfy ||c_k|| < R",
  "any extra loss term or hyperparameter (contrastive, uniformity, hyperbolic regulariser, learned curvature): the loss is the baseline one and kappa is frozen at -1/R^2",
  "curvature, radii or Sinkhorn at levels 2..L, and any change to the deeper argmins, their codebooks or their interfaces: they stay exactly Euclidean and exactly baseline",
  "reparameterising E1 or any codebook as points of the ball, tangent-space training of the encoder, and a Frechet mean or exp/log maps beyond the origin exponentials written above",
  "learning the radii, T_i, R or the behaviour signal by backpropagation, and recomputing the counts from validation or test data: the table is a frozen precompute from the TRAINING split",
  "changes to the decoder, to the Stage-3 input format, and to the straight-through convention: they are the baseline ones and the decoder receives the Euclidean codeword E1[k1]"
 ],
 "continuous_surface": {
  "name": "poincare_level1_distance",
  "callable": "level1_metric:poincare_level1_distance",
  "symbols": [
   "x0",
   "x1",
   "e0",
   "e1"
  ],
  "args": [
   {
    "name": "x",
    "width": 2,
    "radius": 0.0,
    "scalar": 0.0
   },
   {
    "name": "e",
    "width": 2,
    "radius": 0.0,
    "scalar": 0.0
   },
   {
    "name": "T_eff",
    "width": 1,
    "radius": 0.0,
    "scalar": 0.0
   },
   {
    "name": "R",
    "width": 1,
    "radius": 0.0,
    "scalar": 0.0
   },
   {
    "name": "T_max",
    "width": 1,
    "radius": 0.0,
    "scalar": 0.0
   },
   {
    "name": "eps",
    "width": 1,
    "radius": 0.0,
    "scalar": 0.0
   }
  ],
  "statements": [
   "nz = sqrt(x0**2 + x1**2)",
   "zh0 = x0/Max(nz, eps)",
   "zh1 = x1/Max(nz, eps)",
   "Te = Min(T_eff, T_max)",
   "rr = R*tanh(Te/(2*R))",
   "u0 = rr*zh0",
   "u1 = rr*zh1",
   "ne = sqrt(e0**2 + e1**2)",
   "tc = ne/(2*R)",
   "thc = Piecewise((1, Eq(ne, 0)), (tanh(tc)/tc, True))",
   "c0 = e0*thc/2",
   "c1 = e1*thc/2",
   "u2 = u0**2 + u1**2",
   "c2 = c0**2 + c1**2",
   "den = (R**2 - u2)*(R**2 - c2)",
   "arg = 1 + 2*R**2*((u0 - c0)**2 + (u1 - c1)**2)/den",
   "d = R*acosh(arg)"
  ],
  "output": "d",
